## Core Services

### 1. notificationService

**Location**: [services/notificationService.ts](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/notificationService.ts)

#### Methods

##### [createNotification(notification)](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/notificationService.ts#20-30)

Creates a new notification in Firestore.

```typescript
await notificationService.createNotification({
  userId: photoOwnerId,
  type: 'like',
  actorId: currentUser.id,
  actorName: currentUser.name,
  actorAvatar: currentUser.avatar,
  message: `liked your memory.`,
  photoId: photoId,
  createdAt: Date.now(),
  isRead: false
});
```

**Implementation**:
- ✅ Allows self-notifications (user can be notified of their own actions)
- ✅ Writes directly to `notifications` Firestore collection
- ✅ No validation against duplicate notifications

##### [subscribeToNotifications(userId, callback)](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/notificationService.ts#31-51)

Real-time subscription to user's notifications.

```typescript
const unsubscribe = notificationService.subscribeToNotifications(
  userId, 
  (notifications) => {
    setNotifications(notifications);
  }
);
```

**Implementation**:
- Uses Firestore `onSnapshot` for real-time updates
- Queries by `userId`, ordered by `createdAt DESC`
- Returns unsubscribe function for cleanup

##### [markAsRead(notificationId)](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/notificationService.ts#52-60)

Marks a single notification as read.

```typescript
await notificationService.markAsRead(notificationId);
```

##### [markAllAsRead(userId)](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/notificationService.ts#61-84)

Marks all unread notifications for a user as read using batch updates.

```typescript
await notificationService.markAllAsRead(userId);
```

**Implementation**:
- Queries all unread notifications (`isRead == false`)
- Uses Firestore batch write for performance
- Returns immediately if no unread notifications exist

---

### 2. emailService

**Location**: [services/emailService.ts](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/emailService.ts)

#### Methods

##### [sendNotificationEmailBackground(toEmail, toName, type, data)](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/emailService.ts#56-96)

Queues an email notification via Firestore mail collection (trigger-based email sending).

```typescript
await emailService.sendNotificationEmailBackground(
  owner.email,
  owner.name,
  'like',
  {
    actorName: currentUser.name,
    message: "Liked your memory",
    photoUrl: window.location.href
  }
);
```

**Supported Types**:
- `comment` | `tag` | `mention` | `accept_invite` | `like`

**Email Content**:
- Subject: `"New {type} on Famoria"`
- HTML template with action button
- Direct link to photo/content

**Backend Integration**:
- Writes to Firestore [mail](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/emailService.ts#6-55) collection
- Email sending handled by backend Cloud Function or extension
- Non-blocking, fire-and-forget approach

