## Database Structure

### Firestore Collections

#### `notifications` Collection

```
notifications/
├── {notificationId1}
│   ├── userId: "user123"
│   ├── type: "like"
│   ├── actorId: "user456"
│   ├── actorName: "John Doe"
│   ├── actorAvatar: "https://..."
│   ├── message: "liked your memory."
│   ├── photoId: "photo789"
│   ├── createdAt: 1704783600000
│   └── isRead: false
├── {notificationId2}
│   └── ...
```

**Indexes Required**:
- Composite index: `userId ASC, createdAt DESC`
- Composite index: `userId ASC, isRead ASC` (for markAllAsRead)

#### [mail](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/emailService.ts#6-55) Collection (Email Queue)

```
mail/
├── {mailId1}
│   ├── to: ["user@example.com"]
│   ├── message:
│   │   ├── subject: "New like on Famoria"
│   │   ├── text: "..."
│   │   └── html: "<div>...</div>"
│   ├── metadata: { ... }
│   └── createdAt: 1704783600000
```

**Backend Processing**:
- Processed by Cloud Functions or Firestore extensions
- Documents are deleted after successful delivery
- Failed deliveries are logged with error fields

