## Notification Flow Diagrams

### Like Notification Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant LikeButton
    participant notificationService
    participant emailService
    participant Firestore
    participant PhotoOwner

    User->>LikeButton: Click like
    LikeButton->>notificationService: createNotification()
    notificationService->>Firestore: Write to notifications/
    Firestore-->>PhotoOwner: Real-time update
    LikeButton->>emailService: sendNotificationEmailBackground()
    emailService->>Firestore: Write to mail/
    Note over Firestore: Cloud Function processes email
```

### Tag Notification Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Uploader
    participant photoService
    participant notificationService
    participant emailService
    participant TaggedUsers

    Uploader->>photoService: Upload with tags
    photoService->>photoService: notifyTaggedUsers()
    loop For each tagged user
        photoService->>notificationService: createNotification()
        photoService->>emailService: sendNotificationEmailBackground()
    end
    notificationService->>TaggedUsers: Real-time notifications
```

---

## Best Practices

### 1. Error Handling

All notification calls use try-catch to prevent blocking main flows:

```typescript
try {
  await notificationService.createNotification({ ... });
  await emailService.sendNotificationEmailBackground(...);
} catch (err) {
  console.warn("Failed to send notification", err);
  // Continue - notification failure shouldn't break the main action
}
```

### 2. Performance Optimization

- **Batch updates**: Use [markAllAsRead](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/notificationService.ts#61-84) with batch writes
- **Fire-and-forget**: Email sending is async via queue
- **Real-time updates**: Firestore snapshots provide instant UI updates
- **Optimistic UI**: UI updates before server confirmation

### 3. User Experience

- **Self-notifications allowed**: Users can see their own tags/actions
- **Unread indicators**: Clear visual feedback for new notifications
- **Auto-mark read**: Clicking a notification marks it as read
- **Relative timestamps**: "2m ago" is more readable than absolute time
- **Click-outside close**: Dropdown closes on outside clicks

---

## Configuration

### Firestore Security Rules

```javascript
// notifications collection
match /notifications/{notificationId} {
  // Users can read their own notifications
  allow read: if request.auth != null 
              && request.auth.uid == resource.data.userId;
  
  // Anyone authenticated can create notifications
  allow create: if request.auth != null;
  
  // Users can update their own notifications (mark as read)
  allow update: if request.auth != null 
                && request.auth.uid == resource.data.userId;
}
```

### Email Templates

Email templates are embedded in [emailService.ts](file:///Users/gowthamrajsrinivasan/Downloads/famoria%202/services/emailService.ts) and use inline styles for compatibility.

**Customization Points**:
- Subject line format
- HTML template structure
- Button styling
- Footer text
- Color scheme

